UX Brief V1: Fubo Mobile Homepage
Context
The Fubo mobile homepage relies heavily on carousels to surface content. Currently, carousels use a variety of renderers and aspect ratios without a clear organizing principle, leading to visual sameness and potential user confusion. With support for ~30 carousels on screen, we need a coherent strategy that both clarifies what each carousel is for and encourages daily, habitual usage.

Goals
Clarify Intent: Help users instantly understand the purpose of each carousel (Utility vs. Live vs. Editorial).
Drive Habitual Use: Make the homepage a daily destination by highlighting live and short-form sports content effectively.
Enforce Coherence: Establish a scalable structure for ~30 carousels that feels intentional, not cluttered.
Stay Within System: Only leverage existing renderers/components.

Constraints
Carousel Types: Three categories: Utility, Live, and Editorial (note: you listed “Utility” twice — assuming one is “Editorial” or equivalent).
Renderers: Existing components only; no net-new engineering work on modules. Renderers include:
16:9 Small, Medium, Large (16:9 only),  2:3
Rules:
Each carousel must use a single aspect ratio or size.
2:3 aspect ratio reserved for short-form sports content (GameStream).
Opportunity exists for an embedded large player carousel (single 16:9 item).


