Approach 2: Mixed but Differentiated by Aspect Ratio: Use visual differentiation instead of strict stacking to communicate function.

Description: n: Interleave carousels by relevance; aspect ratios signal intent (2:3 = short form, 16:9 small = utility, medium/large = live).
User Stories
As a highlights-first fan, I want clips to look visually distinct so I know what’s snackable
As a new user, I want carousels to “look different” so I can easily scan for my interests.
Use Cases
Mid-day scroll: user taps a 2:3 highlight because it pops visually.
Utility carousels remain legible through consistent 16:9 small formatting.
Pros
Dynamic, less monotonous.
Visual language teaches intent.
Easier to slot in new content types.
Cons
Requires user learning.
Can feel visually noisy.
KPIs
Highlight CTR from 2:3 blocks.
Discovery engagement on editorial picks.
Higher total watch minutes from mix of utility + live.

